WEBVTT

00:00:09.672 --> 00:00:13.258
We will start two counting jobs, then wait until both

00:00:13.258 --> 00:00:14.477
results are ready.

00:00:14.477 --> 00:00:18.131
A thread is a separate path of execution within a Java

00:00:18.131 --> 00:00:18.672
process.

00:00:42.633 --> 00:00:45.772
Runnable supplies work through its run method.

00:00:45.772 --> 00:00:48.228
Each CountJob owns a separate total.

00:00:48.228 --> 00:00:51.639
Its loop increases that total until it reaches the

00:00:51.639 --> 00:00:52.458
job's limit.

00:00:52.817 --> 00:00:55.571
Each start schedules work on a new thread.

00:00:55.571 --> 00:00:59.046
Calling run directly would be an ordinary call on the

00:00:59.046 --> 00:01:00.029
current thread.

00:01:00.029 --> 00:01:02.914
We start both workers before joining either.

00:01:02.914 --> 00:01:05.864
Each join waits for its own target to finish.

00:01:05.864 --> 00:01:09.339
The execution paths may take turns or run at the same

00:01:09.339 --> 00:01:09.667
time.

00:01:09.772 --> 00:01:13.029
Predict the two totals and whether either worker is

00:01:13.029 --> 00:01:15.072
alive when the last line prints.

00:01:15.072 --> 00:01:18.073
Does the first printed result prove that worker

00:01:18.073 --> 00:01:19.031
finished first?

00:01:19.031 --> 00:01:20.372
Pause before running.

00:01:26.622 --> 00:01:29.883
The totals are three and two, and neither worker is

00:01:29.883 --> 00:01:30.267
alive.

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:33.528
Both joins returned normally before the caller read

00:01:33.528 --> 00:01:34.296
the results.

00:01:34.296 --> 00:01:36.726
The caller prints First before Second.

00:01:36.726 --> 00:01:40.051
This output does not establish which worker finished

00:01:40.051 --> 00:01:42.097
first or show a speed advantage.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.519
A Thread can be started once.

00:01:44.519 --> 00:01:47.153
A new attempt needs new Thread objects.

00:01:47.153 --> 00:01:50.733
Rerunning this complete program creates both jobs and

00:01:50.733 --> 00:01:54.110
their workers again, so each total begins at zero.

00:01:54.495 --> 00:01:57.799
If only the second limit becomes five, which output

00:01:57.799 --> 00:02:01.039
lines would change, and which would stay the same?

00:02:01.039 --> 00:02:03.695
Explain why both join calls still matter.
